1 NOTE Died at the hands of AGuaybana II during battle in the town of Sotomayor he founded in 1511.
2 CONT He was born in Spain and arrived August 1509 in Santo Domingo with Diego Columbus.
2 CONT In the same year he went to Isla de San Juan de Puerto Rico with Juan Ceron who was later appointed governor in 1510.
2 CONT His accomplishments:
2 CONT Founded Tavara in what was a mosquito ridden swamp. Tavara was named in honor of his mother, Teresa de Tavora.
2 CONT The people who would have been the co founders of Tavara had to abandon the fledging town because of the ferosity of the mosquitos.
2 CONT Murdered Guarinex in battle.
2 CONT ES.41091.AGI/1.16403.15.413//INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.405V    
2 CONT Titulo Nombre atribuido:
2 CONT Repartimiento de indios
2 CONT Fecha Creacion:
2 CONT 1515-03-21, (Tordesillas)  -  
2 CONT Signatura antigua: INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.171v
2 CONT Signatura Historico:
2 CONT INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.171V
2 CONT Real Cedula al Adelantado Juan Ponce de Leon y al licenciado Velazquez, repartidores de los indios de la isla de San Juan, para que encomienden a D. Pedro de Sotomayor los indios que tenia su padre D. Cristobal de Sotomayor, difun
2 CONC to, como merced por los servicios de este, y entretanto llega D. Pedro a la isla, tenga los indios el contador Antonio Sedeno
2 CONT Research Copyright 2009, John J. Browne Ayes. All Rights Reserved, National And International.
