2 CONT Henry II (13 January 1334 – 29 May 1379), called Henry of Trastámara or the Fratricidal (el Fratricida), was the first King of Castile and León from the House of Trastámara. He became king in 1369 by defeating his half-brother Pet
2 CONC er the Cruel, after numerous rebellions and battles. As king he was involved in the Fernandine Wars and the Hundred Years' War.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He had several children outside wedlock, some of which he mentioned in his will dated 29 May 1374:[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Constanza Enríquez de Castilla. Her father did not mention her mother's name. When he wrote the will in 1374, she was engaged to Infante Denis, Lord of Cifuentes (1354–1397). However she eventually married his brother, Infante J
2 CONC ohn, Duke of Valencia de Campos (1349–1387). She inherited Alba de Tormes.
2 CONT * Pedro Enríquez de Castilla (?-1366). He is buried in Segovia Cathedral.
