1 NOTE History tells us that Guanina was given to Cristobal de Sotomayor.
2 CONT It is said that eventually she became in love with him. When her brother swore to her he would kill the Spanish and his plans for a big battle against the Spanish she informed Cristobal de Sotomayor. As he prepared to leave for ba
2 CONC ttle she begged him not to go.  Its is said that she committed suicide and was found lying upon the breast of her lover. Lucky for her because she was being sought out for sacrifice to the gods as a traitor to her people.
2 CONT Some also say that AGuaybana was so angered that he burned down a town or two.
2 CONT The man who carried the surname, sotomayor, was one of  those would be "conquerors" of Puerto Rico.
2 CONT I have serious doubts concerning the verity within the legends that have arisen around the conquistadors love for their Indian women.  Guanina was "given" to sotomayor and this could only mean that she was given to him as chattle,
2 CONC  like giving a fine horse to a friend foir some perverted deed that he had accomplished. No doubt their "relationship" was one of master over his slave. Therefore there was no love between them because the relationship was one of 
2 CONC rape against a victim.
2 CONT I also doubt that Guanina told her master about the plans that her beloved brother had made to attack the Spaniards. Why would a slave who was being raped and enslaved be on sotomayor's side?
2 CONT I think its time we take a long hard look at those, "legends."
2 CONT Ayes
