1 NOTE Rey de Portugal y Algarbe (1325-1357)
1 NOTE Rey de Portugal y Algarbe (1325-1357)
1 NOTE     ES II:39
1 NOTE Alfonso IV, called The Brave (1290-1357), king of Portugal (1325-57), the 
2 CONT son of Diniz, whom he succeeded, and grandson of Alfonso III. He ordered 
2 CONT the murder of Ines de Castro, the wife of his son Dom Pedro (1320-67). She 
2 CONT was a member of the Castilian royal family, and Alfonso IV feared the 
2 CONT marriage would hurt Portugal politically.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "THE BRAVE"; KING OF PORTUGAL
1 NOTE King of Portugal
