1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pedro Enríquez de Castilla y Angulo de Córdoba (circa 1352 - Orense, 1400), Conde de Trastámara.
2 CONT
2 CONT =========================
2 CONT
2 CONT * Pedro Enriquez de Castilla, conde de Trastamara 
2 CONT * 1355+ Orense 02.05.1400 
2 CONT * Parents 
2 CONT * Father: Fadrique Alfonso de Castilla, señor de Haro * 1335  
2 CONT * Mother: N 
2 CONT * Marriages 
2 CONT * 1385  D. Isabel de Castro * c. 1360  
2 CONT * Children 
2 CONT * Fadrique de Castilla, duque de Arjona * 1388  [married] Aldonza de Mendoza María de Guzmán 
2 CONT * Enrique de Castilla [married] Leonor Alvarez de Robleda 
2 CONT * Alfonso de Castilla  
2 CONT * Fernando de Castilla  
2 CONT * Luis de Castilla  
2 CONT * Beatriz de Castro * c. 1400 [married] Diego Lopez de Avalos [& ]Pedro Alvarez Osorio, Conde de Lemos 
2 CONT * Biographical NotesData only available to Geneall Plus registered users. 
2 CONT * Please Login or read access conditions. 
2 CONT * Titles 
2 CONT * Counts of Trastamara  
2 CONT * Occupations 
2 CONT * Constables of Castilla (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geneall.net/H/per_page.php?id=1103
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Constable of Castile (Spanish: Condestable de Castilla) was a title created by John I, King of Castile in 1382, to substitute the title '''Alférez Mayor del Reino'''. The constable was the second person in power in the kingdom, af
2 CONC ter the King, and his responsibility was to command the military in the absence of the ruler. In 1473 Henry IV of Castile made the title hereditary for the Velasco family and the Dukes of Frías. After these changes, the title ceas
2 CONC ed to have any military or administrative connotations, and was simply an honorific title.
2 CONT --------------------
