1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eleanor of Alburquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Alburquerque (1374 - 1435) became Queen consort of Aragon by her marriage to Ferdinand I of Aragon. In Spanish she is known as Leonor Urraca de Castilla, Condesa de Alburquerque.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was Sancho of Alburquerque, who was an illegitimate son of King Alfonso XI of Castile and his mistress Eleanor of Guzman, and a brother of King Henry II of Castile. Her mother was Infanta Beatriz, Countess of Alburquerq
2 CONC ue, who was daughter of Peter I of Portugal and Ines de Castro.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1394 she married her husband. They had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso V of Aragon (1394-1458), also king of Sicily and Naples
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Aragon, first wife of John II of Castile, (1396-1445)
2 CONT
2 CONT John II of Aragon (1397-1479)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry of Aragon, Duke of Alburquerque, Count of Villena, Count of Empuries and Grand Master of the Order of Santiago (1400-1445)
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon (Queen of Portugal), who married Edward I of Portugal (1402-1445)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella of Aragon, Countess of Urgel, who married Pedro, duke of Coimbra
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro of Aragon, Count of Alburquerque and Duke of Noto (1406-1438)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho of Aragon (1410-1416)
2 CONT
