0 @N6000000002244391721@ NOTE Bastard son of John I who married the daughter of constable Nono Alvares.
1 CONT Their descendants, the House of Braganca, became kings of Portugal from 1640.
1 CONT From this Alfonso on, the title of Duke of Braganca was borne by the heir
1 CONT presumptive (father to son, to son, etc. usually). This dynasty was finally
1 CONT restored in the revolution, or restoration, in 1640 with the crowning of John
1 CONT IV, the 8th Duke of Braganca, as King of Portugal, after 60 years of Spanish
1 CONT rule. This dynasty ruled 'til the end of the reign of Maria II in 1853.
